{
  "sn1.20:0.1": "Linked Discourses 1.20 ",
  "sn1.20:0.2": "2. The Garden of Delight ",
  "sn1.20:0.3": "With Samiddhi ",
  "sn1.20:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "sn1.20:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Rājagaha in the Hot Springs Monastery. ",
  "sn1.20:1.3": "Then Venerable Samiddhi rose at the crack of dawn and went to the hot springs to bathe. ",
  "sn1.20:1.4": "When he had bathed and emerged from the water he stood in one robe drying his limbs. ",
  "sn1.20:1.5": "Then, late at night, a glorious deity, lighting up the entire hot springs, went up to Samiddhi, and, standing in the air, addressed him in verse: ",
  "sn1.20:2.1": "“Mendicant, you seek alms before you eat; ",
  "sn1.20:2.2": "you don’t seek alms after eating. ",
  "sn1.20:2.3": "But you should eat first, then seek alms: ",
  "sn1.20:2.4": "don’t let the time pass you by.” ",
  "sn1.20:3.1": "“I actually don’t know the time; ",
  "sn1.20:3.2": "it’s hidden and unseen. ",
  "sn1.20:3.3": "That’s why I seek alms before eating, ",
  "sn1.20:3.4": "so that the time may not pass me by!” ",
  "sn1.20:4.1": "Then that deity landed on the ground and said to Samiddhi, ",
  "sn1.20:4.2": "“You’ve gone forth while young, mendicant. With pristine black hair, you’re blessed with youth, in the prime of life, and you’ve never flirted with sensual pleasures. ",
  "sn1.20:4.3": "Enjoy human sensual pleasures! ",
  "sn1.20:4.4": "Don’t give up what is apparent in the present to chase after what takes effect over time.�